@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# AUDIT REPORT 2026-10-25T14-33-21Z-414
+PATCH: audits/pending_patch.diff
+FILES: .github/workflows/build-meson.yml, .opencode/agents/sil3_auditor.md, prompts/PROMPT-audit.md, scripts/agent_up.sh, tools/agents/coordinator/AGENTS.md, tools/agents/coordinator/opencode.json, tools/agents/fence/README.md, tools/agents/fence/base.json, tools/agents/fence/roles/auditor.json, tools/agents/fence/roles/coordinator.json, tools/agents/fence/roles/dev.json, tools/agents/fence/roles/qe.json, tools/agents/render_fence.py, tools/agents/roles/README.md, tools/agents/roles/auditor.json, tools/agents/roles/coordinator.json, tools/agents/roles/dev.json, tools/agents/roles/qe.json, tools/agents/twins/nexios-audit.md, tools/agents/twins/nexios-dev.md, tools/agents/twins/nexios-qe.md, tools/agents/verify_fence.py, tools/check_no_cross_edits.sh
+
+## FINDINGS
+- [S1] scripts/agent_up.sh:503 — mode_run has no role allowlist (rejects only `*/*` and `*.json`).
+  WHY: `run <sess> <dir> evil <prompt>` passes the guard, so any slash-free role string reaches run_session, where the disk-trust hole below turns it into a live session.
+- [S1] scripts/agent_up.sh:540 — run_session trusts `$RENDERED_ROOT/<role>/opencode.resolved.json` on disk (`[ -s ]` only) and never invokes the renderer for the role.
+  WHY: a pre-planted config (writable via bash, which bypasses opencode permission maps by design) launches as a live session and check_fenced passes, because it asserts consistency of the four env values, not provenance of the config.
+- [S2] scripts/agent_up.sh:224 — install_agents renders dev/qe/auditor only, while run_session's comment claims it "renders every role, including this one".
+  WHY: `run ... coordinator ...` silently reuses a possibly-stale coordinator config with a stale `{repo}` expansion after a repo move, defeating the S3-2R moved-clone fix through this path (silent adoption of stale state, the exact mode prune_link hard-fails elsewhere).
+- [S3] scripts/agent_up.sh:1122 — mode_launch_cmd (`__run-cmd`) reaches rendered_path/mkdir before any role validation.
+  WHY: `__run-cmd ../../../tmp/x` runs `mkdir -p` outside RENDERED_ROOT before the renderer rejects the role — launch stays fail-closed but an unvalidated role string causes a filesystem side effect.
+- [S3] tools/agents/render_fence.py:189 + tools/agents/verify_fence.py:124 — renderer does not confine delta allow keys to declared namespaces, and F5 checks external_directory only, never edit.
+  WHY: a well-formed delta `edit_allow` of `/etc/cron.d/x` (non-/tmp, so no mirror is required) renders clean and passes the verifier, so fence-widening is caught only by human review, never by a gate.
+- [S3] tools/agents/verify_fence.py:180 — F8 generates fresh twins into a temp dir and checks those; on-disk agent files are never inspected and F7 covers configs only.
+  WHY: a stale or hand-weakened on-disk twin (e.g. `bash: allow` in `<cwd>/.opencode/agents/sil3_auditor.md`) is invisible to the gate; self-containment is proven for the generator, not the artifact.
+- [S3] tools/agents/render_fence.py:181 + tools/agents/verify_fence.py:86 — rendered auditor session keeps `permission.bash "allow"` while its subagent twin carries the ask + git/diff/grep map, and neither emit_twin's parse-back nor F8 compares bash.
+  WHY: if ask-everywhere is the intent, the live auditor session does not implement it; if session-allow is intended, the asymmetry drifts silently past both guards — needs an owner decision, so no unilateral fix.
+- [S4] tools/agents/render_fence.py:246 — write_atomic uses O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC without O_EXCL/O_NOFOLLOW on a predictable pid-suffixed temp name.
+  WHY: a pre-created symlink at `<path>.tmp.<pid>` redirects the write through the link (same-user model, no secret values in the file, so hardening only).
+- [S4] scripts/agent_up.sh:548 + scripts/agent_up.sh:584 — unquoted `$tdir`/`$cfg` in the remote env command; `tr ' ' '\n'` env tokenization in check_fenced.
+  WHY: paths with spaces split and fail the fence match, killing a healthy session (fail-closed, confusing, not a defusal).
+
+## PATCH
+`audits/rejected_patch.diff` was written and `git apply --check` passes; it allowlists the role in mode_run, run_session and __run-cmd and makes run_session re-render the role via render_role_config instead of trusting the file on disk.
+
+DECISION: REJECTED
