+# AUDIT REPORT 2026-10-25T14-45-14Z-414-iter2
+PATCH: audits/pending_patch.diff
+FILES: .github/workflows/build-meson.yml, .opencode/agents/sil3_auditor.md, prompts/PROMPT-audit.md, scripts/agent_up.sh, tools/agents/coordinator/AGENTS.md, tools/agents/coordinator/opencode.json, tools/agents/fence/README.md, tools/agents/fence/base.json, tools/agents/fence/roles/auditor.json, tools/agents/fence/roles/coordinator.json, tools/agents/fence/roles/dev.json, tools/agents/fence/roles/qe.json, tools/agents/render_fence.py, tools/agents/roles/README.md, tools/agents/roles/auditor.json, tools/agents/roles/coordinator.json, tools/agents/roles/dev.json, tools/agents/roles/qe.json, tools/agents/twins/nexios-audit.md, tools/agents/twins/nexios-dev.md, tools/agents/twins/nexios-qe.md, tools/agents/verify_fence.py, tools/check_no_cross_edits.sh
+
+## ITER-1 DISPOSITIONS (all verified in worktree + re-run, no trust in claims)
+- [S1] mode_run allowlist -- CLOSED. scripts/agent_up.sh:503 allowlists dev|qe|auditor|coordinator; self-test refuses `evil` and `coordinator/../dev` (re-ran 64/64 PASS).
+- [S1] run_session disk-trust -- CLOSED. scripts/agent_up.sh:543-544 re-renders THIS role via render_role_config (fail-closed) instead of `[ -s ]` on disk; comment states the never-trust-disk invariant.
+- [S2] coordinator stale via run path -- CLOSED. Same re-render covers `run ... coordinator`; ensure_coord_session also renders coordinator fresh (:632) before reuse-assert.
+- [S3] __run-cmd mkdir-before-validation -- CLOSED. mode_launch_cmd allowlists first (:1146); render_role_config fails on the missing delta file before any mkdir; `test -e /tmp/agentup-evil` refusal probe passes.
+- [S3] delta allow unconfined + F5 edit-blind -- CLOSED. validate_delta_paths covers edit_allow/edit_deny/external_allow, rejects absolute paths outside namespace roots and any hand-typed /private prefix; F5 iterates both sections; N14 (/etc/cron.d/x) and N15 (/private/tmp/...) abort (re-ran render-self-test 46/46).
+- [S3] F8 fresh-only twins -- CLOSED. check_agents compares full content of on-disk copies under $NEXIOS_HOME/rendered/<role>/ (STALE on difference) and asserts the twin bash map equals delta agent.bash when dict (re-ran verify_fence OK + --self-test 8/8 bite).
+- [S3] auditor bash asymmetry -- CLOSED as owner decision with mechanical enforcement both sides: F2 pins every session bash to allow; emit_twin parse-back + F8 pin the twin bash to agent.bash. Residual prose gap recorded as S3-2 below.
+- [S4] write_atomic predictable tmp -- CLOSED. O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW + os.urandom(6) suffix, 0600, fsync, atomic replace.
+- [S4] whitespace/substring env -- CLOSED. Whitespace in any launcher-injected env value fails closed on both launch paths; check_fenced decides by substring on the raw `ps eww` environment (tokenized view diagnostic only).
+- Check-7 retrieval -- COVERED. Issue #414 work-begun comment carries graphify query + obsidian search with dispositions for this subsystem; iter-2 touches no new subsystem.
+
+## FINDINGS
+- [S3] tools/agents/fence/README.md:78 -- stale verification counts ("44 checks", "13 fail-closed probes").
+  WHY: render-self-test is 46/46 with N1-N15 (15 probes); the doc undercounts both, so a future count drop looks intentional.
+- [S3] tools/agents/fence/roles/auditor.json:22 -- twin bash-map narrowing vs pre-#414 is undocumented, and the session-allow vs twin-ask owner decision has no prose home.
+  WHY: echo/cat/tail/wc allows were dropped (fail-closed direction, Read tool covers files) and both sides are machine-pinned, but only code states the intent; one README paragraph should record the decision so a future "restore" is not mistaken for drift.
+- [S3] tools/check_no_cross_edits.sh:31 -- change-set gate does not mirror the new map denies (dev bash-writes under tools/agents/fence/** or .opencode/agents/** pass the gate).
+  WHY: the map denies bind only edit/write tools while bash heredocs bypass by design, and the gate is the documented second half; a well-formed malicious namespace addition is property-valid (passes F1-F8), leaving audit/CI-review as the only controls for the highest-value paths.
+
+DECISION: APPROVED
